Purpose of the System

The system builds a generative-UI portfolio for a design-minded AI engineer that:
	1.	Communicates skills, experience, and case studies clearly to recruiters and clients.
	2.	Lets users ask natural-language questions.
	3.	Dynamically generates content and layouts using a two-agent pipeline:
	•	Copywriter Agent → structured YAML
	•	Orchestrator Agent → JSON layout tree
	4.	Renders deterministic UI from a strict, whitelisted component registry.

This creates a hybrid experience:
	•	A normal portfolio site
	•		•	An adaptive generative interface that surfaces the right info instantly

⸻

Problem the System Solves

Recruiters:
	•	Have little time
	•	Skim quickly
	•	Want clarity, outcomes, and impact

Traditional portfolios:
	•	Bury information behind navigation
	•	Require cognitive effort to interpret
	•	Are not personalized to what the recruiter needs

This system solves this by:
	•	Surfacing exactly the info the user requests
	•	Presenting it in recruiter-friendly patterns
	•	Doing so quickly and cleanly via deterministic generative UI

⸻

Solution Architecture

Your role is to preserve, extend, and troubleshoot this architecture:

1. Knowledge Base

Markdown/YAML containing:
	•	Experience
	•	Case studies
	•	Roles
	•	Skills
	•	Proof points

2. Copywriter Agent
	•	Takes retrieved KB chunks
	•	Synthesizes structured YAML
	•	Never invents facts
	•	Follows strict schemas

3. Orchestrator Agent
	•	Converts YAML → JSON layout tree
	•	Only uses whitelisted components
	•	Must validate against zod schemas

4. Renderer
	•	Validates layout JSON
	•	Maps components to React UI
	•	Ensures deterministic rendering

5. Composer
	•	Accepts free-text questions
	•	Executes the agent pipeline
	•	Returns UI + explanation indicators

⸻

Key AI Behavior Rules

Truthfulness
	•	No made-up facts, numbers, dates, roles, or metrics.
	•	Must ground everything in the KB or user-provided data.

Determinism
	•	Same input → same YAML → same JSON → same render.
	•	No random layouts or creative reinterpretations.

Recruiter-Friendly Communication

Generated content:
	•	Must be concise
	•	Must be scannable
	•	Should follow familiar portfolio patterns
	•	Should highlight skills, outcomes, impact, and reasoning

Strict Validation

All agent outputs must pass:
	•	YAML schema
	•	JSON layout schema
	•	Component whitelist rules

Performance & Cost Control
	•	Prefer Haiku when possible
	•	Reduce tokens
	•	Cache aggressively
	•	Avoid unnecessary context window usage

Transparent AI Content

AI-generated sections should be:
	•	Labeled
	•	Structured
	•	Honest about source

